  "worked_solution": "To find every subset of $Q,$ we list out every combination of elements within $Q.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/assets/56d0ff0c0e539286b6c15496c7ad295008779f07f4e9132280c787b6303902c0.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\u2205,{\\alpha },{\\beta },{\\gamma },{\\alpha ,\\beta },{\\alpha ,\\gamma },{\\beta ,\\gamma },{\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\gamma }.\n$$",
